Prompt_Falling_Sand

Create a 2D grid-based falling sand simulation (cellular automaton), in a single self-contained HTML file. No external libraries: everything inline, rendered on a canvas.
Requirements:
A pixel-art style grid of at least 200x200 cells scaled up to fit the screen.
Four selectable materials for the user to paint with using the mouse: Sand, Water, Wood, and Fire.
Physics rules: Sand falls down and slides down diagonal slopes. Water spreads out horizontally and falls. Wood is static.
Interaction rules: Fire burns Wood (turns it to empty space over a few frames). Water puts out Fire. Sand sinks in Water.
A UI bar at the top or bottom with buttons to select the current drawing material, and a slider to change the brush size.
A live on-screen counter showing active particles (non-empty cells) and frames per second. The update loop must process the grid efficiently from bottom to top to avoid particle tearing.
Output only the complete HTML file.
